---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Colorize & Recolor"
  description="Tint grayscale images, recolor a masked region, constrain a palette, and transfer a reference look locally in Varve."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="colorize-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Colorize &amp; Recolor
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <StatusPill status="available" label="Deterministic workflows available" />
        <h1>Put color back under your control.</h1>
        <p>
          Tint a grayscale image, replace a selected color, work inside a real mask, constrain a
          palette, or borrow the color distribution of a reference. Varve keeps the source image
          intact and makes the scope of every operation visible.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="workflow-grid" aria-label="Colorize workflows">
        <article class="workflow-card workflow-card--accent">
          <span class="workflow-number">01</span>
          <h2>Tint / recolor</h2>
          <p>Set an absolute hue or rotate existing hue relationships. Neutral grayscale pixels receive chroma instead of staying gray.</p>
          <span class="workflow-meta">Offline · no model required</span>
        </article>
        <article class="workflow-card">
          <span class="workflow-number">02</span>
          <h2>Palette colorize</h2>
          <p>Choose document swatches and decide whether you want shaded tonal influence or literal palette colors.</p>
          <span class="workflow-meta">Shaded or strict mapping</span>
        </article>
        <article class="workflow-card">
          <span class="workflow-number">03</span>
          <h2>Reference transfer</h2>
          <p>Use a separate image's global color statistics while retaining the target's structure and source coverage.</p>
          <span class="workflow-meta">Statistical · not semantic matching</span>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="review-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Review before commit</p>
        <h2 id="review-title">A preview is a proposal, not a replacement.</h2>
        <p>
          Preview runs at the quality mode&apos;s model resolution and includes a split-view
          comparator against the original. Apply creates a new embedded result layer, rebuilds the
          approved colors over the full-resolution source, and leaves the original image available
          for comparison, undo, export, and another pass. A changed source, mask, reference,
          palette, or control signature cannot be overwritten by late asynchronous work.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section split-section" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Scope you can see</p>
          <h2 id="scope-title">Masks are inputs, not instructions.</h2>
          <p>
            Whole-image scope is explicit. Mask scope requires an actual image mask, keeps its
            dimensions, and resamples coverage at source pixel centres. Blend and feathering are
            applied once, so zero coverage remains the source.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="contract-list">
          <div><strong>Lightness</strong><span>CIELAB L* preservation, not an unlabeled HSL slider.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Protection</strong><span>Conservative heuristics are labelled; a user mask remains authoritative.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Transparency</strong><span>Alpha and transparent source pixels stay intact.</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section photo-note" aria-labelledby="photo-title">
        <div class="photo-note__status"><StatusPill status="partial" label="Photo AI: model-gated" /></div>
        <h2 id="photo-title">Photo colorization, without pretending it recovered history.</h2>
        <p>
          Varve has a local DDColor adapter for plausible photo colorization. It is enabled only
          when a verified model is installed and compatible with the current runtime. The model
          predicts chroma at a bounded working size; Varve reconstructs the result with the
          original source lightness, detail, and alpha. If the artifact is missing, deterministic
          tint and recolor still work and no source image is uploaded as a fallback.
        </p>
        <p class="photo-note__small">
          Varve records the official acquisition route, but the configured release assets are not
          currently published. DDColor ONNX bytes still require independent integrity and visual
          verification before this lane is advertised as ready. <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/colorization')}>Read the readiness notes.</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <aside class="honesty" aria-labelledby="honesty-title">
        <h2 id="honesty-title">Designed around the failures people notice.</h2>
        <p>
          No hidden whole-image recolor when a mask is missing. No fake strict palette mode that
          produces colors outside the palette. No cloud-only requirement for a tint. No accepted
          result that disappears on reopen. Review the output where leaks, neutral drift, alpha
          fringes, and low-resolution softness would actually show up.
        </p>
        <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/colorization')}>Read the Colorize workflow guide →</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <a href={sitePath('/download')} class="btn-default">Download Varve</a>
        <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/colorization')} class="btn-secondary">Open the guide</a>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .colorize-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .page-hero { max-width: 740px; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .page-hero h1 { margin: 1rem 0; font: 700 clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem)/1.05 var(--font-editorial); color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .page-hero p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .workflow-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .workflow-card { min-height: 230px; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-card); }
  .workflow-card--accent { border-color: var(--border-accent); background: var(--surface-accent-soft); }
  .workflow-number { color: var(--text-tertiary); font: .75rem var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .workflow-card h2 { margin: 2.5rem 0 .75rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .workflow-card p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
  .workflow-meta { display: block; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .8rem; }
  .feature-section { margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .feature-section h2, .honesty h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.3rem); margin: .5rem 0 1rem; }
  .feature-section p, .honesty p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; }
  .split-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr .9fr; gap: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 4rem; }
  .contract-list { display: grid; gap: .75rem; align-content: start; }
  .contract-list div { display: grid; gap: .3rem; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-surface); }
  .contract-list strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .contract-list span { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; font-size: .92rem; }
  .photo-note { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding: 1.5rem 0 1.5rem 1.25rem; }
  .photo-note__status { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .photo-note__small { font-size: .9rem; }
  .photo-note a, .honesty a { color: var(--text-link); font-weight: 600; }
  .honesty { border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-card); padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 2rem; }
  .btn-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: .7rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-control); color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .workflow-grid, .split-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .workflow-card { min-height: auto; } .workflow-card h2 { margin-top: 1.5rem; } }
</style>
